questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a batch data synchronization service fails with `java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space` after processing approximately 200,000 records. The service runs on OpenJDK 17 with 4GB heap and default G1GC settings. Here is the relevant code snippet:

java
@Service
public class TransactionExportService {
    @PersistenceContext
    private EntityManager entityManager;

    @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRED)
    public void exportBatch(List<Long> transactionIds, OutputStream destination) {
        for (int i = 0; i < transactionIds.size(); i++) {
            Transaction tx = entityManager.find(Transaction.class, transactionIds.get(i));
            writeToStream(destination, tx);
            if (i % 1000 == 0) {
                entityManager.flush();
            }
        }
    }
}


Heap dump analysis indicates that millions of `Transaction` entity instances and their associated dirty-checking snapshots are retained in memory despite the periodic `entityManager.flush()` calls.
